WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.999 --> 00:00:14.019
found a wormhole?"

2
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:15.060
Zann exclaimed.

3
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.721
"In Swamp Bottom?"

4
00:00:17.602 --> 00:00:19.643
"Uh-huh." Perda looked pleased with herself.

5
00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:23.406
"See, I've been practicing some spells since we got home.

6
00:00:24.366 --> 00:00:26.488
Mostly Seeking spells and a few others."

7
00:00:26.908 --> 00:00:27.468
She shrugged.

8
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:32.812
"I've been thinking I might want to be an explorer someday, so I want to be ready."

9
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.700
Zann was surprised.

10
00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.881
Since when did Perda want to be an explorer?

11
00:00:39.142 --> 00:00:41.022
But he didn't have time to think about that right now.

12
00:00:41.042 --> 00:00:42.803
"So what happened?"

13
00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:43.603
he asked.

14
00:00:44.063 --> 00:00:45.463
"How did you find the wormhole?"

15
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:51.525
"I was using the Seeking spell to find the strongest sources of magic in Swamp Bottom," Perda said.

16
00:00:51.545 --> 00:00:59.507
"Mostly the spell pointed me to the spots I expected— City Hall, your house, the spellstone quarry, places

17
00:00:59.547 --> 00:00:59.947
like that.

18
00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.268
But there was one source I couldn't identify.

19
00:01:04.348 --> 00:01:08.030
I went and checked it out, and that's when I found the wormhole."

20
00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:11.391
"Wow!" Zann was impressed.

21
00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:16.873
Seeking spells were advanced magic—he didn't have any idea how to perform one himself.

22
00:01:16.893 --> 00:01:19.414
"And you're sure it's a wormhole?"

23
00:01:19.654 --> 00:01:20.074
he added.

24
00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:21.875
"Of course I'm sure!

25
00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:24.516
It's small and kind of unstable-looking.

26
00:01:25.457 --> 00:01:29.258
It's probably brand-new, which is why nobody else has noticed it yet."

27
00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:31.159
Zann's head spun.

28
00:01:31.639 --> 00:01:33.280
This changed everything!

29
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.241
"You have to show me," he said.

30
00:01:36.261 --> 00:01:37.462
"I will."

31
00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:38.463
Perda smiled.

32
00:01:38.863 --> 00:01:41.225
"But only if you'll let me come with you."

33
00:01:41.245 --> 00:01:42.686
"Come with me?

34
00:01:43.166 --> 00:01:44.787
You mean, through the wormhole?"

35
00:01:44.807 --> 00:01:48.369
"Yes." Perda's eyes shone with excitement.

36
00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.391
"I want to see what the vortex is like.

37
00:01:51.852 --> 00:01:54.233
I want to help you search all those other worlds."

38
00:01:55.394 --> 00:01:56.395
Zann shook his head.

39
00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.896
"I can't let you come.

40
00:01:58.376 --> 00:01:59.477
It's too dangerous!"

41
00:02:00.638 --> 00:02:01.898
Perda folded her arms.

42
00:02:01.918 --> 00:02:03.840
"I don't care if it's dangerous.

43
00:02:04.576 --> 00:02:05.317
That's my deal.

44
00:02:05.757 --> 00:02:06.858
Take it or leave it."

45
00:02:07.838 --> 00:02:08.719
Zann bit his lip.

46
00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:11.941
For a second he was tempted to agree to her deal.

47
00:02:12.722 --> 00:02:15.644
Perda was smart and brave and good at magic.

48
00:02:16.505 --> 00:02:18.406
It could be helpful to have her along.

49
00:02:19.226 --> 00:02:22.769
Then Zann remembered all the adventures they'd been through together lately.

50
00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.972
No, he couldn't put Perda in that kind of danger again.

51
00:02:27.752 --> 00:02:31.195
This was his quest, and he should be the only one to take the risks.

52
00:02:32.136 --> 00:02:36.021
Still, he couldn't pass up this chance to find a wormhole close to home.

53
00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:39.822
"It's a deal," he said, trying to sound sincere.

54
00:02:39.842 --> 00:02:41.543
"You can come along."

55
00:02:42.263 --> 00:02:43.603
"Cool!" Perda grinned.

56
00:02:44.903 --> 00:02:47.964
Zann forced a smile, though he already felt guilty.

57
00:02:48.705 --> 00:02:50.245
He hated lying to Perda.

58
00:02:51.105 --> 00:02:54.546
And he knew she was going to be furious when she figured out that he'd tricked her.

59
00:02:55.286 --> 00:02:56.987
But what other choice did he have?

60
00:02:57.787 --> 00:03:00.628
He just had to hope that she would forgive him someday.

61
00:03:01.896 --> 00:03:03.977
"Let's go check out the wormhole," he said.

62
00:03:03.997 --> 00:03:05.297
"Right now?"

63
00:03:05.778 --> 00:03:06.918
She sounded surprised.

64
00:03:06.938 --> 00:03:09.799
"Shouldn't we gather some supplies first?

65
00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.921
Professor Huli says some other worlds don't have the same kind of magic we do.

66
00:03:15.882 --> 00:03:20.444
So we can't count on just creating anything we need, like food or extra clothes."

67
00:03:21.904 --> 00:03:23.765
"Oh, we aren't going right now."

68
00:03:24.485 --> 00:03:25.566
Zann thought fast.

69
00:03:25.586 --> 00:03:28.247
"We should go tomorrow after school.

70
00:03:28.707 --> 00:03:31.108
That will give us plenty of time to gather supplies."

71
00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:34.185
"Tomorrow?" Perda frowned.

72
00:03:34.205 --> 00:03:35.887
"Why not later today?"

73
00:03:35.907 --> 00:03:41.290
"Um, well, it might take some time to find the supplies we need.

74
00:03:41.971 --> 00:03:42.891
We don't want to rush."

75
00:03:43.972 --> 00:03:45.573
Perda didn't say anything for a second.

76
00:03:45.973 --> 00:03:46.954
Zann held his breath.

77
00:03:47.755 --> 00:03:50.296
He needed her to think they were really going tomorrow.

78
00:03:51.337 --> 00:03:54.999
That would give him plenty of time to sneak back to the wormhole later today.

79
00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:58.582
"Okay, I guess that makes sense," she said at last.

80
00:03:58.602 --> 00:04:00.343
"We'll go tomorrow."

81
00:04:00.363 --> 00:04:02.605
"Great. Now where is it?"

82
00:04:02.625 --> 00:04:04.186
"It's this way."

83
00:04:06.728 --> 00:04:08.610
Perda zapped them both out of the swamp.

84
00:04:09.651 --> 00:04:12.433
They landed on the street a few blocks from Zann's house.

85
00:04:13.314 --> 00:04:16.456
From there they walked to a wooded area at the edge of town.

86
00:04:17.537 --> 00:04:21.100
In the middle of a small clearing was a ripple of magic energy.

87
00:04:21.981 --> 00:04:25.524
When Zann and Perda stepped closer, it opened into a wormhole!

88
00:04:25.544 --> 00:04:28.587
"Wow," Zann said, staring at it.

89
00:04:29.427 --> 00:04:34.477
It was small, just as Perda had said—much smaller than the ones in First City.

90
00:04:35.557 --> 00:04:42.239
The edges sparked and swirled wildly, and the opening changed size and shape every few seconds.

91
00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:49.601
Zann jumped back as the wormhole let out a small burst of magic energy, sucking in some fallen

92
00:04:49.661 --> 00:04:52.462
leaves. Perda took a step closer.

93
00:04:52.482 --> 00:04:55.663
"Are you sure you don't want to go today?"

94
00:04:55.683 --> 00:04:58.344
"I'm sure," Zann said quickly.

95
00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:03.342
"Let's each pack a bag to take with us, and then hide the bags in the swamp.

96
00:05:04.382 --> 00:05:06.203
We can meet there after school tomorrow."

97
00:05:07.044 --> 00:05:10.625
"Zann! Come here, please!"

98
00:05:10.985 --> 00:05:11.626
Boz called.

99
00:05:12.386 --> 00:05:15.327
Zann was in his room stuffing things into a backpack.

100
00:05:16.147 --> 00:05:18.669
He shoved it under his bed and hurried out of the room.

101
00:05:19.469 --> 00:05:21.130
Boz was standing near the front door.

102
00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.770
"What is it?"

103
00:05:23.371 --> 00:05:26.292
Zann tried to sound normal even though he was nervous.

104
00:05:27.372 --> 00:05:29.313
Could Boz have figured out what was going on?

105
00:05:30.094 --> 00:05:32.555
But Boz looked distracted, as usual lately.

106
00:05:32.575 --> 00:05:35.737
"I have a meeting with the mayor," he said.

107
00:05:35.757 --> 00:05:37.718
"But I'll be home for dinner."

108
00:05:37.738 --> 00:05:39.839
"Okay," Zann said.

109
00:05:40.399 --> 00:05:41.200
"I'll see you then."

110
00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.081
"Good." Boz smiled at him.

111
00:05:44.101 --> 00:05:50.525
"We've both been so busy since returning from the capital that I feel I've hardly seen you.

112
00:05:51.285 --> 00:05:54.227
Perhaps we can finally have that talk this evening."

113
00:05:54.907 --> 00:05:58.245
Boz zapped out of sight, and Zann slumped with relief.

114
00:05:59.245 --> 00:06:01.726
This could be his chance to go back to that wormhole.

115
00:06:02.586 --> 00:06:04.567
He just had one thing to do first.

116
00:06:04.587 --> 00:06:06.428
"Come on, boy."

117
00:06:06.908 --> 00:06:08.029
Zann whistled for Zing.

118
00:06:08.049 --> 00:06:10.750
"Let's go see Darb."

119
00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.471
Zing stared at him and let out a puff of smoke.

120
00:06:15.131 --> 00:06:16.572
But the dragon stayed where he was.

121
00:06:16.592 --> 00:06:18.613
"What's wrong with you?"

122
00:06:19.013 --> 00:06:21.034
Zann said impatiently, grabbing Zing.

123
00:06:21.754 --> 00:06:22.314
"Let's go!"

124
00:06:23.375 --> 00:06:26.056
Zann snapped his fingers and zapped out of the house.

125
00:06:26.969 --> 00:06:31.190
Once Zing was safe with Darb, there would be nothing standing in Zann's way.
